1947
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:29,150
...would definitely be the first answer I received.

1948
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:33,410
<i>He's correct, that surely sounds
like something I'd say at the time.</i>

1949
00:08:34,110 --> 00:08:36,120
My deepest apologies.

1950
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:40,790
Well, you apologizing for that puts me
in an awkward position...

1951
00:08:41,210 --> 00:08:45,990
But at least in the end you finally
showed more interest in me than in books.

1952
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:50,430
Isn't that right?

1953
00:08:55,850 --> 00:09:00,140
I worried you even more when I was with Irene.

1954
00:09:00,810 --> 00:09:04,940
Both Glen and Alex investigated Lady Irene,
but not only was nothing found,

1955
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:09,360
the threat to your safety began.

1956
00:09:11,230 --> 00:09:17,290
So, I decided to find out for myself.
Your aunt worked with us as well.

1957
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:21,710
Huh? Then, my aunt's illness was...

1958
00:09:21,710 --> 00:09:25,380
Right. It was an excuse to get you away from the palace.

1959
00:09:30,190 --> 00:09:33,760
But it wound up causing
a terrible misunderstanding with you in the end.

1960
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:40,140
At that time, my mind went completely blank.

1961
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:44,980
Well... thanks to that you were able to realize
how you truly felt.

1962
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:55,490
But... I truly regret the fact that I hurt you deeply.

1963
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:02,000
This <i>is</i> a book that I sought out for you...

1964
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:08,040
and I <i>did</i> want to see your face full of joy.

1965
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:16,390
Will you...

1966
00:10:17,050 --> 00:10:19,140
accept it once more?

1967
00:10:22,730 --> 00:10:27,600
<i>"There's no special meaning in gifts from the prince."</i>

1968
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:32,060
<i>That's what I believed that day.</i>

1969
00:10:34,580 --> 00:10:35,760
<i>But...</i>

1970
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:40,990
Yes.

1971
00:10:45,210 --> 00:10:49,960
Thank you, Prince Christopher.

1972
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:55,480
Eli.

1973
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:58,200
Your Highness...

1974
00:11:06,490 --> 00:11:11,520
What exactly is this "hidden name" my family has?

1975
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:19,030
You could have saved that question for later, Eli...

1976
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:21,360
Huh?

1977
00:11:22,750 --> 00:11:25,660
Is Prince Christopher out again?

1978
00:11:26,030 --> 00:11:29,170
Yes. He was heading towards the royal library earlier.

1979
00:11:29,170 --> 00:11:33,420
I tried to stop him, but it seemed there
was something on his mind today.

1980
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:35,410
He could use some manners.

1981
00:11:41,610 --> 00:11:42,430
I did it!

1982
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:47,440
Apologize!

1983
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:51,470
Apologize to the book!

1984
00:11:54,730 --> 00:11:56,990
Excuse you! Do you know
who you're talking to with such a—

1985
00:11:56,990 --> 00:11:59,450
It doesn't matter who you are!

1986
00:11:59,450 --> 00:12:03,740
Books are the words of our now silent ancestors.
They are humanity's treasures.

1987
00:12:03,740 --> 00:12:09,420
Were you taught that it was okay
to be cruel to those who can't speak?

1988
00:12:10,290 --> 00:12:13,290
You're exaggerating way too much.
It's only a book, you know.

1989
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:16,620
"Only?"

1990
00:12:21,930 --> 00:12:24,220
How old are you?

1991
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:25,720
T-Twelve.

1992
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:31,770
This book that you threw was written
over a hundred years ago,

1993
00:12:31,770 --> 00:12:34,900
and it is a historical document that
even now continues to be reprinted.

1994
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:36,030
So wha—

1995
00:12:36,030 --> 00:12:42,450
And people like you who have only lived twelve years
are practically a baby compared to this book.

1996
00:12:42,450 --> 00:12:46,120
A freshly hatched baby chick
that still hasn't escaped its shell.

1997
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,180
A... baby... chick?

1998
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:49,290
Now apologize to our great ancestors!

1999
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:55,040
I-I'm sorry.

2000
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:28,670
What are you reading?

2001
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:32,960
Are you here to do violence to another book?

2002
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:35,670
I won't do it anymore.

2003
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:42,430
What's that book?

2004
00:13:42,430 --> 00:13:45,190
Legends from a country in the east.

2005
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:49,100
Is it good?

2006
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:52,100
Yes.

2007
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:44,490
You wish to speak about your engagement?

2008
00:14:44,490 --> 00:14:46,360
To the daughter of the Marquess.

2009
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:48,880
And what is the young lady's name?

2010
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:56,120
No sooner had I said the name,
than my father and the prime minister started to panic.

2011
00:14:56,470 --> 00:15:00,610
Oh dear. Was it a person of noble status?

2012
00:15:02,690 --> 00:15:04,090
Eli...

2013
00:15:04,090 --> 00:15:04,630
Yes.

2014
00:15:05,290 --> 00:15:09,430
I'm talking about <i>our</i> past together right now.

2015
00:15:09,430 --> 00:15:10,440
Huh?

2016
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:14,380
You mean, even with all that said, you don't remember?

2017
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:16,920
I-I sincerely apologize.

2018
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:22,940
Well, I did think I'd made the worst possible impression on you,
so perhaps this is fortunate...

2019
00:15:25,210 --> 00:15:33,330
Anyways, that was the first time I heard the secret name of
"the brains of Sauslind" in relation to the Bernstein family.

2020
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:38,920
It's an alias known only to people of the royal family
and a small part of the palace.

2021
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:41,460
The brains.... of Sauslind?

2022
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:47,620
The kings whom the Bernsteins had directly served
all had equally prosperous reigns.

2023
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:54,850
Your father and your brother Alfred
are both highly valued for those abilities.

2024
00:15:54,890 --> 00:15:58,310
However, because it is the nature of the Bernstein family,

2025
00:15:58,310 --> 00:16:01,770
the two of them chose to live buried in books
than rise to prominence.

2026
00:16:01,770 --> 00:16:03,070
Wow.

2027
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:09,660
It is living surrounded by books
that can be said to be the source of those high abilities.

2028
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:17,040
The fact that they don't put weight on their ability
is a virtue of the Bernstein family,

2029
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,900
and also a fault.

2030
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:22,170
It's an honor to be told this, but...

2031
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:27,670
I thought that my family was simply generations
of a group of people who loved books.

2032
00:16:28,410 --> 00:16:32,460
Do you remember when you spotted
that Zelger as a fake?

2033
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:33,350
Yes.

2034
00:16:33,350 --> 00:16:34,180
That time as well.

2035
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:40,150
In an art book, it said that the Zelger
is considered a royal treasure

2036
00:16:40,150 --> 00:16:42,530
because it uses an ore that is no longer available,

2037
00:16:42,530 --> 00:16:48,110
and the color called "Zelger blue"
that is produced by a unique mixture is highly valued.

2038
00:16:48,110 --> 00:16:55,240
"Zelger" means "dawn" in the ancient language.
Basically, "Zelger blue" is the rich blue found at dawn.

2039
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:59,750
It appears to be a solid color,
and according to an old book, the crest also...

2040
00:16:59,750 --> 00:17:04,130
Alex and I marveled at your family,
full of extensive knowledge.

2041
00:16:59,750 --> 00:17:01,830
Yes, it's subtle.

2042
00:17:04,710 --> 00:17:08,760
That's just something I knew from reading a book.

2043
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:15,390
But there's more. The embezzlement situation in Weimar,
and the stability of diplomatic relations with Maldura,

2044
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:18,440
both happened due to your advice.

2045
00:17:20,450 --> 00:17:23,310
You are quite the "Brain of Sauslind"...

2046
00:17:23,310 --> 00:17:26,150
You yourself proved it.

2047
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:32,410
But, an engagement with the Bernstein family,
who does not pander to authority is difficult...

2048
00:17:32,410 --> 00:17:39,910
My father and the prime minister both warned me
there may be a chance the request could hurt your family.

2049
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:48,670
Refusing to back down, I ignored their warnings and advice,
and immediately approached Marquess Bernstein.

2050
00:17:51,140 --> 00:17:52,680
Then...

2051
00:17:54,210 --> 00:17:58,680
The next day, you had disappeared
from the royal capital.

2052
00:17:59,070 --> 00:18:01,810
You had returned to your family's estates.

2053
00:18:02,190 --> 00:18:03,560
Oh...

2054
00:18:03,970 --> 00:18:06,560
My thoughtlessness at that time...

2055
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:10,320
I truly wish I could shove myself down from behind.

2056
00:18:10,810 --> 00:18:15,820
<i>Your Highness... I fairly certain it's impossible
to shove yourself down from behind... </i><i></i>

2057
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:19,490
After that, my appeals to the Marquess
were constantly rejected.

2058
00:18:19,490 --> 00:18:23,410
When you were finally introduced into society,
and I thought we could finally meet again...

2059
00:18:23,410 --> 00:18:30,460
you didn't remember me at all, and you'd return
the same greeting no matter who addressed you.

2060
00:18:31,050 --> 00:18:34,550
<i>Your Highness, that's what people normally do. </i><i></i>

2061
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,430
I apologize for my rudeness...

2062
00:18:44,090 --> 00:18:45,050
Eli.

2063
00:18:47,030 --> 00:18:51,940
Though you may be the "Phantom of the Library",
or a "fairy princess", or too dull,

2064
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:54,780
my feelings won't change.

2065
00:18:57,610 --> 00:19:00,130
At last, I have you.

2066
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:05,250
At this point, no matter what happens,
I have no intention of letting you go.

2067
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:13,250
<i>I can feel His Highness' emotions.</i>

2068
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:21,010
<i>He doesn't want the Bernstein name...
He wants me, personally.</i>

2069
00:19:21,650 --> 00:19:24,270
<i>But, but...</i>

2070
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:29,060
But, I haven't taken any proper training to be a princess.

2071
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:33,440
Here is what my mother and the court ladies
are already saying concerning that:

2072
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:39,140
Your knowledge, education, etiquette, appearance,
and temperament are all great.

2073
00:19:40,010 --> 00:19:42,830
Huh? I-I...

2074
00:19:42,830 --> 00:19:45,750
I'm not good at navigating high society.

2075
00:19:45,750 --> 00:19:47,360
That isn't true.

2076
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:54,710
When entertaining foreign guests,
Mother made sure to let you sit with them, right?

2077
00:19:54,710 --> 00:20:00,010
Your knowledge of culture and language
concerning foreign countries has been a huge help.

2078
00:20:00,010 --> 00:20:01,690
I don't believe that...

2079
00:20:01,690 --> 00:20:05,020
That's just the role of the fiancée of the crown prince.

2080
00:20:05,020 --> 00:20:11,720
Eli. You are firmly building your own
place here, with your own power.

2081
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,970
<i>He has too much to say after my rebuttals...</i>

2082
00:20:14,860 --> 00:20:18,530
<i>I can't help but feel like I'm being rolled
around in the prince's hand.</i>

2083
00:20:20,070 --> 00:20:21,030
<i>But...</i>

2084
00:20:22,780 --> 00:20:30,920
<i>I feel that the uneasiness that was in my chest,
the burden of being a phony fiancée, is fading away.</i>

2085
00:20:31,380 --> 00:20:37,050
Eli. Perfection may be demanded
from those with elevated status, but luckily,

2086
00:20:37,530 --> 00:20:43,050
there are people around us who make up for that.

2087
00:20:43,570 --> 00:20:49,190
But more than any of that I want you
to be by my side, now and forever.

2088
00:20:51,490 --> 00:20:53,690
Don't you want that, Eli?

2089
00:21:03,290 --> 00:21:08,580
Is it really okay... for me to be by your side?

2090
00:21:10,810 --> 00:21:13,960
Eli... Elianna.

2091
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:22,220
You are the only one I want by my side, eternally.

2092
00:21:27,370 --> 00:21:29,980
<i>I understand clearly now.</i>

2093
00:21:31,110 --> 00:21:36,730
<i>These four years, the time that
I spent in my normal routine,</i>

2094
00:21:36,730 --> 00:21:44,130
<i>that was something irreplaceable to me...
I never wanted to lose it.</i>

2095
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:55,750
For the first time, I've realized that there's a world
that I can't understand through books alone.

2096
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:59,000
Eli.

2097
00:21:59,610 --> 00:22:01,480
My beloved...

2098
00:22:04,050 --> 00:22:05,790
bibliophile princess.

